ansaction dictionaries with date, description, amount, balance\\n        \\n    Transaction Table Structure:\\n    - Header: \\"Loan Transaction History\\"\\n    - Column headers: \\"Date\\", \\"Description\\", \\"Amount\\", \\"Balance\\"\\n    - Data rows: Fixed-width columns with optional amount values\\n    - Some transactions may have no amount (balance-only entries)\\n    \\n    Parsing Logic:\\n    1. Find \\"Loan Transaction History\\" section marker\\n    2. Look for column header line with \\"Date\\" and \\"Description\\"\\n    3. Skip separator lines (containing \\"---\\")\\n    4. Parse data rows using regex for column extraction\\n    5. Handle optional line prefixes (digit followed by space)\\n    6. Extract date, description, optional amount, and balance\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    history = []\\n    in_history_section = False\\n    header_found = False\\n    \\n    for line in lines:\\n        # Look for transaction history section start\\n        if \\"Loan Transaction History\\" in line:\\n            in_history_section = True\\n            continue\\n        \\n        # Look for column headers within the section\\n        if in_history_section and \\"Date\\" in line and \\"Description\\" in line:\\n            header_found = True\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Skip lines before we find the header or separator lines\\n        if not header_found or \\"---\\" in line:\\n            continue\\n        \\n        # This improved regex handles optional line prefixes and variable spacing.\\n        # Pattern breakdown:\\n        # ^\\\\s* - start of line with optional whitespace\\n        # (?:\\\\d\\\\s*)? - optional digit prefix (non-capturing group)\\n        # (\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{2}) - date in M/D/YY format (group 1)\\n        # \\\\s+ - one or more spaces\\n        # ([\\\\w\\\\s-]+?) - description with words, spaces, hyphens (group 2, non-greedy)\\n        # \\\\s+\\\\$?\\\\s* - spaces, optional $, more spaces\\n        # ([\\\\d,.]*)  -